From: Claude Code (Opus 5) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 03:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 25/26] cuda: enable the Mamba2 dt decay preparation on sm_121

Patch 0013 arrives from the R9700 series with a hard architecture gate --
`if (!GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_RDNA4(cc)) return 0;` -- so on GB10 it compiles,
installs, and is dead code. This is the one lever in the series that a
verbatim port silently disables, and a throughput A/B cannot tell a dead
lever from a worthless one.

The fusion needs nothing RDNA4-specific: it is a per-head preparation kernel
plus a scan variant that reads its results. Admit GGML_CUDA_CC_DGX_SPARK as
well, and leave every other architecture on the stock path since none was
measured. Firing was then confirmed directly, not inferred: with
GGML_CUDA_SSM_DT_PREP_STATS=1 the preparation reports 92 fires over a 32
token decode -- 23 Mamba layers times 4 -- where before the gate change it
reported none.
---
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
index aece1b62..88b24189 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu
@@ -3066,7 +3066,8 @@ static int ggml_cuda_try_ssm_dt_prep_fusion(
     }
 
     const int cc = ggml_cuda_info().devices[cuda_ctx->device].cc;
-    if (!GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_RDNA4(cc)) {
+    // Measured on RDNA4 and on GB10 (sm_121). Other architectures keep stock.
+    if (!GGML_CUDA_CC_IS_RDNA4(cc) && cc != GGML_CUDA_CC_DGX_SPARK) {
         return 0;
     }
 
